        "h2": "Keep everyone informed",
        "content": "Same-day work changes the day for other customers too. If adding a job pushes a scheduled pickup back an hour, that customer should hear about it before they start wondering.\n\nFor the new customer, a confirmation with the time window, then an on-the-way text when the crew heads over, and a tech-arrived text when they pull up. Same-day customers are often stressed and on a deadline, so frequent updates calm them down. For the rest of the route, an on-the-way text tells each customer when their crew is actually coming.\n\nIf a day falls apart, such as a truck breaking down, rescheduling a day sends each customer on it a reschedule text. That beats a dozen phone calls from the cab of a broken truck."
